2026-06-09 20:36:25,748 | INFO | Response: Disciplinary actions for not reporting to office (such as habitual late attendance, habitual leave, absence without leave, overstaying leave without obtaining consent, or going on leave without proper authorization) can include:

- Progressive disciplinary action as listed in section 3.2 and point 4.1 (not shown in your context but referred).
- Factors influencing the action: history of misconduct, gravity of misconduct, employee response, work history (section 3.3).
- For specific misconduct such as habitual late attendance, habitual leave, or absence without leave, this is classified as Level I (LI) misconduct (see table).
